    id: 58,
    letter: "O",
    topic: "ok",
    titulo: "Ok",
    audioUrl: "https://listenaminute.com/o/ok.mp3",
    pageUrl: "https://listenaminute.com/o/ok.html",
    fullTranscript: `I like the expression OK. I don't know why. It's so useful. Everyone in the world understands what it means. It must be the only word that everyone knows. Is it a word or is it an abbreviation? We spell it okay but abbreviate it as OK. I wonder how many meanings it has. You can ask if someone is OK if they are ill; you can ask if someone understands a question or instructions using OK; you can even let someone know enough is enough by saying OK. If you say something is OK, it means you don't really like or dislike it. In fact, sometimes, if you say he's OK or she's OK, it means you don't really like them. I think okay is also a verb. I have heard people say, It's OK, John okayed it.`,
